        "source_evidence": {
          "unit_id": "L0003",
          "start": 64,
          "end": 805,
          "quote": "**Justification:** FDISCO is specifically selected because it is a solvent-based clearing method that provides excellent transparency for 3 mm brain blocks while uniquely utilizing low temperature (4 ℃) and alkaline pH adjustment (pH 9.0 via TEA) during dehydration. This specifically prevents the quenching of weak endogenous fluorescent proteins (like GFP), allowing for high-resolution 3D morphological analysis of fine dendritic structures and long-term storage (months) without signal loss. The dual-target strategy utilizes the preserved endogenous GFP to trace sparse neurons, while DAPI serves as a nuclear counterstain to provide essential 3D anatomical context without requiring complex immunolabeling that might damage the tissue.",
